   "desc": "A Middle Jurassic forest floor in the dark, walked by ear. The nine ensiferans of Gu et al. 2026 sing, and the sound changes as you move because the physics says it should — ISO 9613 atmospheric absorption and dense-foliage scattering over spherical spreading, inverted by bisection to draw each singer’s audible radius on the map. The synthesiser is the animal: a bandlimited impulse train at the tooth-strike rate driving a two-pole resonator at the mirror-cell frequency, so syllable length is not a parameter but falls out of teeth × spacing / strike rate. The file is a shape rather than a number — the published inter-tooth spacing curves are the paper’s actual argument, so Archaboilus warbles and Allaboilus clicks-then-bursts on their own. The Rust kernel holds no palaeontology and the palaeontology holds no physics; every value carries a provenance tag rendered beside it, and the selftest fails if a carrier stops claiming published. The pitch is theirs; the rhythm is ours, and the page says so.",
