     "desc": "Conway's Game of Life on a Voronoi mesh of a torus. B3/S23 is really a fact about squares having eight neighbours, so here the rule is a fraction of whatever neighbourhood a cell drew — four to eight sides, six on average, exactly six on average because Euler says so. Roll sites, relax the mesh, then roll soups until one refuses to settle: the hunt scores every trajectory and shows you the duds it rejected. Six found specimens ship with the page, including one that never repeated in 5000 generations and one whose period-210 attractor is just lcm(2,3,5,6,14) of oscillators ignoring each other. Every universe is a seed, so every good one is a URL.",
