     "desc": "A square filling a cube. Pixel (x, y) is coloured by a continuous map from the square onto the RGB cube, which cannot be smoother than Hölder 2/3 and, since August 2026, need not be worse (Arnold’s problem 1988–5, solved by Badger–Palmer). Rendered on the GPU: every colour appears equally often — exactly, to the pixel, at the lattice sizes — and no two neighbours differ by more than two levels, with no seams and the same surface at every zoom. A seed bends it with area-preserving maps of the torus, so the histogram stays flat and every image is a URL; the census tab counts the claims and the print tab hands you a 4096² PNG that is the census.",
