   "desc": "Bismuth hopper crystals, grown rather than drawn. A seeded colony of mason agents lays one brick at a time under three rules from real crystal growth — Kossel kinetics, the Berg effect, anisotropy — and a stepped, hollow, right-angled hopper emerges. The iridescence is thin-film interference computed per pixel. Same seed, same crystal, forever. Every specimen has a quasicrystal cousin grown on a Penrose or other plane tiling and an icosahedral cousin grown on golden rhombohedra, the three-dimensional quasicrystal; /lab is the playground: pick the substrate, paint the initial condition, rewrite the brain's laws, breed or thin the colony, release worms. /study is the two-agent phase space, measured.",
