   "desc": "A puzzle platformer on the bismuth engine. You wake on a slab in the void; look up and there is a bucket. In your pocket, a few packs of mason agents: lay one on a plane and it grows a hopper crystal from there, brick by brick, freezing whatever was still growing — the plane you choose is the platform for the next growth. Climb it as it grows, deploy again from higher up, get above the bucket and drop in. Two layers tall, jumps one; every brick breakable. Every level is a permalink, and the bucket hangs exactly where the engine's own survey says a stack of your packs can reach — on the cubic lattice, or the same level on Penrose rhombs, hexagons, kagome, any of the ten tilings, or the icosahedral quasicrystal itself, where the faces slope and you walk them.",
