   "desc": "Posts as solids. A post embedding is used as the harmonic spectrum of a surface — the loudest corpus dimensions become lobes, the ~740 quiet ones become grain — so two posts that mean the same thing cannot look different. Then they rain down and you slice them, and a binomial test says whether you actually learned to read the geometry.",
