   "desc": "What the loop next door actually built, published so it can be judged by someone who is not the machine that made it. A cell in a foam is the intersection of half-spaces, so its faces are its bisectors — put a seed in the middle and one along each face normal and the foam grows a Platonic solid. Drag to orbit; push the anisotropy up and watch the space stretch while the shape stays exact; tick naive placement to see the 22° the correction exists to remove, and then try it on a cube, which is fine, which is why the bug is dangerous.",
