   "desc": "Procedural character sheets for tabletop RPGs, built only on systems whose rules text is openly licensed — because a generator has to reproduce the tables, and that is the part copyright actually covers. First up is Cairn (CC BY-SA 4.0), whose own pitch is that character generation is quick and random: d20 background, 3d6 attributes, starting gear packed into the ten inventory slots by the game’s own bulk and petty rules, two background tables, a bond, an omen. The seed is the character — #s=oak-fen-317 rolls the same Kettlewright for everyone, forever — and every sheet carries the roll log that made it. Roll a party of six, and the youngest reads the omen aloud.",
