   "desc": "The open-source card audio player, designed in the open. A Toniebox charges $19.99 a story and a Yoto card $9.99; the tag inside one costs about 20¢, because the tag holds no audio at all — NTAG213 has 144 bytes of user memory and a minute of speech is 180,000. It holds a 64-bit pointer, which is why one card can carry six books and why re-pointing a card never touches the card. Here: the product and site architecture, a browser studio that records a parent reading and writes the tag over Web NFC, and a simulator of the box so the whole thing can be got wrong before any solder is bought.",
